    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Omalizumab:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " anti-IgE. Mepolizumab, benralizumab: block IL-5 or its receptor (IL-5 drives eosinophilic airway inflam). Dupilumab: blocks IL-4Rα (IL-4 and IL-13). Tezepelumab: blocks TSLP."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Asthma:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " severe asthma refractory to step-up therapy (USU ↑dose ICS + LABA) w ↑IgE or eosinophils. Omalizumab: severe allergic asthma w ↑ IgE. Mepolizumab works w eosinophils > 150/µL. ⍉for acute bronchospasm or status asthmaticus."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Omalizumab 75–375 mg SC Q2 or 4 wks, by baseline total IgE and wt. Mepolizumab 100 mg SC Q4wks (asthma ≥ 12 y). Benralizumab SC loading then Q8wks. Tezepelumab SC Q4wks."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Anaphylaxis can follow any dose of dupilumab, benralizumab, omalizumab or tezepelumab, even after earlier doses were tolerated (boxed warning: omalizumab); hypersensitivity w mepolizumab. Mepolizumab: herpes zoster (vaccinate first unless contraindicated). Malignancies seen in trials (omalizumab)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Tx pre-existing helminth infect first; if a new one doesn't respond, hold mepolizumab (Nucala) until it resolves. Don't stop systemic or inhaled steroids abruptly when starting; taper gradually if appropriate."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Start omalizumab in a setting equipped to mgnt anaphylaxis and observe after each dose. IgE stays ↑on tx (up to one yr after stopping), so re-testing IgE can't guide dosing."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
